# Telegram Dashboard Bot (Node.js)

This project is a polished Telegram bot built with Node.js and Telegraf. It includes an elegant dashboard layout with inline buttons, fake profile data, fake wallet balance, stats, and smooth callback-based message editing.

Features

- Premium-style dashboard UI
- Inline keyboard navigation
- Profile screen
- Fake wallet balance screen
- Stats screen
- Help screen
- Callback-based edit flow for a clean chat experience
- Safe environment variable config using .env

Setup

1. Install dependencies:

   npm install

2. Create a .env file in the project root:

   TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
   TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

   DERIV_CLIENT_ID=
   # Use only scopes configured for your Deriv OAuth application.
   DERIV_OAUTH_SCOPES=

   # Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
   TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

   # This domain and callback must also be registered with Deriv exactly as shown.
   PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://g-squad.buzz
   PORT=3000
   BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
   # Set true only when the app is reachable exclusively through a trusted HTTPS reverse proxy.
   # That proxy must overwrite X-Forwarded-Proto and X-Forwarded-For.
   TRUST_PROXY=true
   DATABASE_PATH=./data/telegram-deriv.sqlite

3. Start the bot:

   npm start

Commands

- /start — open the dashboard
- /menu — show the main menu

Usage

Send /start or any normal message to the bot, then use the inline buttons to navigate around the dashboard. Every screen is updated in place with callback queries instead of sending a flood of new messages.

Important

- Do not hardcode your real Telegram token into the source code.
- Keep the token inside a local .env file.
- This project uses fake demo values for profile and balance data.

Project structure

- index.js — bot logic and UI flow
- package.json — dependencies and scripts
- .env.example — sample environment file
- .gitignore — excludes environment and local files

